//RS //! D-PIN1=A / D-PIN2=A / D-PIN3=A: the `Pin<T>` address-stability contract.
//RS //! Covers the ratified law end to end:
//RS //!   * `mem.pin(&place)` opens a tracked write window; a value argument is E0218;
//RS //!   * safe code cannot move, replace, or resize a pinned place (E0219);
//RS //!   * reading and editing through the pin stay legal and reach the owner;
//RS //!   * a `Pin<U>` field projects to `Pin<U>` through a pinned value;
//RS //!   * the promise ends with the pin's scope and never escapes its owner;
//RS //!   * AOT and the TIR interpreter agree on every case (I9).
